**Why DTOs?**

```java
// ❌ WITHOUT DTOs: Expose entity directly
@GetMapping("/{id}")
public Offre getOffre(@PathVariable Long id) {
    return offreRepository.findById(id).get();
    // Problems:
    // - Exposes all fields (including images as BLOB)
    // - Can't serialize lazy-loaded collections
    // - Frontend depends on entity structure
    // - Security: Can see fields you shouldn't
}

// ✅ WITH DTOs: Clean API contract
@GetMapping("/{id}")
public OffreResponse getOffre(@PathVariable Long id) {
    Offre offre = offreRepository.findById(id).get();
    return offreMapper.toResponse(offre);
    // Benefits:
    // - Images encoded as Base64 (JSON-safe)
    // - Only include relevant fields
    // - API versioning is easier
    // - Security: Hide internal details
}
```

