## Development Workflow

### Adding a New Feature

**1. Backend:**
```
Create Entity → Create DTO → Create Repository → Create Service → Create Controller → Create Listener (if event-driven)
```

**2. Frontend:**
```
Create Service → Create Component → Add Route → Create Guard (if needed)
```

### Example: Add "Download Offer Details as PDF"

**Backend:**
```java
// 1. Entity (Offre already exists)

// 2. DTO
public record OffreExportDto(
    Long id, String titre, String description, ...
) {}

// 3. Repository (existing)

// 4. Service
@Service
public class OffreExportService {
    public byte[] exportToPdf(Long offreId) {
        Offre offre = offreRepository.findById(offreId).orElseThrow();
        // Generate PDF using iText or Apache PDFBox
        return pdfGenerator.generate(offreMapper.toExportDto(offre));
    }
}

// 5. Controller
@GetMapping("/{id}/export/pdf")
public ResponseEntity<byte[]> exportPdf(@PathVariable Long id) {
    byte[] pdf = offreExportService.exportToPdf(id);
    return ResponseEntity.ok()
        .header("Content-Disposition", "attachment; filename=offre.pdf")
        .body(pdf);
}
```

**Frontend:**
```typescript
// 1. Service
@Injectable({ providedIn: 'root' })
export class OffreExportService {
    constructor(private http: HttpClient) {}
    
    exportPdf(offreId: number) {
        return this.http.get(
            `/api/offres/${offreId}/export/pdf`,
            { responseType: 'blob' }
        );
    }
}

// 2. Component
export class OffreDetailComponent {
    constructor(private exportService: OffreExportService) {}
    
    downloadPdf() {
        this.exportService.exportPdf(this.offreId).subscribe(blob => {
            const url = window.URL.createObjectURL(blob);
            const a = document.createElement('a');
            a.href = url;
            a.download = 'offre.pdf';
            a.click();
        });
    }
}

// 3. Template
<button (click)="downloadPdf()">Download PDF</button>
```

